    "concept": "Virtual Memory - Effective Memory Access Time (EAT) with TLB",
    "markdown": "- **Given Parameters:**\n  - TLB access time ($t_{\\text{TLB}}$) $= 10\\text{ ns}$\n  - Main memory access time ($t_m$) $= 50\\text{ ns}$\n  - TLB hit ratio ($h$) $= 90\\% = 0.9$\n  - TLB miss ratio ($1 - h$) $= 10\\% = 0.1$\n  - Page fault rate $= 0$ (no page faults occur)\n\n- **Access Latency Analysis:**\n  - **Case 1: TLB Hit:**\n    - The frame number is retrieved directly from the TLB, followed by one memory access to fetch the required data word:\n      $$T_{\\text{hit}} = t_{\\text{TLB}} + t_m = 10 + 50 = 60\\text{ ns}$$\n  - **Case 2: TLB Miss:**\n    - The TLB is searched first (miss). Then the page table in main memory is accessed to obtain the frame number, followed by a second memory access to fetch the data word:\n      $$T_{\\text{miss}} = t_{\\text{TLB}} + 2 \\times t_m = 10 + 50 + 50 = 110\\text{ ns}$$\n\n- **Effective Access Time Calculation:**\n  $$\\text{EAT} = h \\times T_{\\text{hit}} + (1 - h) \\times T_{\\text{miss}}$$\n  $$\\text{EAT} = 0.9 \\times 60\\text{ ns} + 0.1 \\times 110\\text{ ns} = 54\\text{ ns} + 11\\text{ ns} = 65\\text{ ns}$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is **Option C (65)**.",
