    "concept": "Network Programming - TCP Sockets & 3-Way Handshake Initiation",
    "markdown": "- **Evaluation of Socket System Calls:**\n  - **`socket()`:** Creates an unbound endpoint for network communication and returns a socket descriptor. No network packets are transmitted.\n  - **`bind()`:** Associates a local IP address and port number with the created socket descriptor. No network packets are transmitted.\n  - **`listen()`:** Puts a stream socket into passive listening mode to accept incoming connection requests. No network packets are transmitted.\n  - **`connect()`:** Invoked by an active client process to establish a TCP connection with a remote server. It initiates the **TCP 3-way handshake** by generating and sending the initial **SYN** packet to the server's listening port.\n\n- **Conclusion:** The `connect()` system call sends the SYN packet.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is **Option D (connect)**.",
